IDEA 1: Concept-balanced DFF — From detached, row-normalized block-8 patch outputs \(Z\), form \([Z_+,(-Z)_+]\); fit rank-8 nonnegative matrix factorization with 10 multiplicative-update iterations, producing concept activations \(H\). Normalize each concept column by its maximum.
Greedily select exactly \(K=\lfloor\text{budget}\rfloor\) distinct patches using marginal scores \(\Delta_i=\sum_c\log(1+H_{ic}/(1+\sum_{j\in S}H_{jc}))\): diminishing returns balance interpretable concepts, potentially preserving bird parts despite background-dominated attention.
— basis: Collins, Achanta & Süsstrunk, [*Deep Feature Factorization for Concept Discovery*, ECCV 2018](https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.10206); signed-feature adaptation and selection objective are proposed here.
— closest prior token-pruning work and difference: [CoverPruner, EMNLP 2026](https://aclanthology.org/2026.emnlp-main.349/) covers query-weighted token representations; this balances discovered student concepts independently of attention, labels, and concept area.
— extra FLOPs: approximately 0.03–0.08 GFLOPs/image for \(d=192\)–384, including factorization and greedy scoring; no additional student forward or gradients. Untested.

IDEA 2: Preserve the Outliers — Using detached, row-normalized block-8 patch outputs \(Z\), approximate \(\min_{\operatorname{rank}(L)\le4,E}\frac12\|Z-L-E\|_F^2+0.25\sum_i\|E_i\|_2\) with five alternating truncated-SVD and row-shrinkage updates; \(e_i=\|E_i\|_2\) explains each patch’s departure from shared internal features.
Keep the highest-\(e_i\) \(\lfloor3K/4\rfloor\) patches; fill the remaining budget from unselected patches by farthest-first Euclidean sampling of \(L_i\), initialized with the patch farthest from their mean, preserving representative shared context alongside exceptional features.
— inspired by: Xu, Caramanis & Sanghavi, [*Robust PCA via Outlier Pursuit*, NeurIPS 2010, arXiv:1010.4237](https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.4237); the bounded rank-constrained solver is an approximation, without the paper’s recovery guarantee.
— why it transfers: Among the retrieved mechanisms, separating whole exceptional feature vectors best matches small bird regions amid repeated background; reinterpret those exceptions as valuable evidence, although clutter can also be exceptional.
— queries tried: recover low rank background sparse foreground robust principal component pursuit; conditional information gain sensor selection correlated observations Gaussian process; invariant rationales explanations spurious correlations feature attribution environment labels; unsupervised discovery rare coherent patterns compression minimum description length paper; contrastive principal component analysis salient variation background dataset 2018; Robust PCA via Outlier Pursuit Xu Caramanis Sanghavi NIPS 2010.
— closest prior token-pruning work and difference: [Beyond Attentive Tokens, CVPR 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.11315) considers attention and rank-one diversity; this explicitly decomposes student computation into shared structure and patch-sparse exceptions, selecting original patches without merging.
— extra FLOPs: roughly 0.02–0.10 GFLOPs/image with bounded randomized rank-4 SVD, \(d=192\)–384; no additional forward or gradients. Both proposals require verification at \(K<98\): near-Full-KD accuracy **and** WGA, plus wins against all six baselines at identical \(K\).